WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00.610 --> 00:04.190
In the scenario we saw earlier in this section with Noah and Aaliyah,

2
00:04.650 --> 00:08.670
we saw them come together to meet for the first time to discuss the transformation.

3
00:09.570 --> 00:11.040
What could Noah have done differently?

4
00:11.970 --> 00:16.160
Luckily, Noah did pivot in the meeting to ask Aaliyah how she was handling everything.

5
00:16.680 --> 00:21.120
Because actually, one way of really demonstrating empathy is asking about other people —

6
00:21.670 --> 00:24.870
not making assumptions about how they’re feeling or thinking about something,

7
00:25.700 --> 00:31.140
and actually just giving them the time and space to explain how they feel, or what they think.

8
00:32.010 --> 00:34.630
And Noah listened in that moment. He really did.

9
00:35.300 --> 00:38.690
And it was the beginning of building a bridge in his relationship with Aaliyah —

10
00:39.270 --> 00:42.470
a constructive relationship, so that they can work happily

11
00:43.080 --> 00:45.359
together throughout the rest of the project.

12
00:45.359 --> 00:48.830
Now, what did Aaliyah do in that meeting that demonstrated empathy?

13
00:49.700 --> 00:52.160
She naturally came in with her own agenda.

14
00:52.490 --> 00:56.670
She was the one who had set the meeting. However, she did ask Noah early on:

15
00:57.090 --> 00:59.140
“Is there anything else you’d like to talk about?”

16
00:59.910 --> 01:05.380
And she created a bit of space there to ensure that there was time for Noah to express what might be on his mind,

17
01:05.860 --> 01:08.420
and that she would be in a position to be able to address some of it.

18
01:09.410 --> 01:13.760
Little steps like that can go a long way to demonstrate empathy in a business context.

